# The demo's user database, in apache's htpasswd format: one username:hash
# per line, lowercase names, and no password anywhere in the PHP.
#
# Both lines are bcrypt at cost 10, which is what `htpasswd -B -C 10` writes.
# The passwords are below because this is a demo that has to be signed in to;
# a deployment keeps its file out of the repository and names it in
# writable_paths of nothing, because nothing writes to it.
#
#   admin  / hunter2hunter2
#   reader / readerreader
#
# phpscript reads this file; the application never does. Adding a user is
# `htpasswd -B -C 10 .htpasswd <name>` and a reload: the `user` table is
# rebuilt from the file by users.php on every start.
admin:$2y$10$DO7HU4Y9f1NKLV5gMS7U5uyprbS5dU5IlZvaAj08tAhjWc7XJB.l2
reader:$2y$10$yKtnzOxpEjs3.wEpk2L9eefs9FG.j8huUfZQ1qfd3S6SF4G0EN61K
